development.solution_text:
At $x = 2$, $f'(2) = 0$, so the derivative has an $x$-intercept at $(2, 0)$.
A cubic with a horizontal point of inflection at $x = 2$ has derivative $f'(x) = k(x - 2)^2$. Since this cubic is increasing, $k > 0$, so $f'(x) > 0$ for all $x \neq 2$.
The derivative graph is a parabola touching the $x$-axis at $(2, 0)$ and opening upwards.
