development.solution_text:
Since $f(x)$ is decreasing for all $x$, $f'(x) < 0$ everywhere (the derivative lies entirely below the $x$-axis).
As $x \to \infty$, the curve flattens out, so $f'(x) \to 0$ from below.
As $x \to -\infty$, the curve becomes steeper, so $f'(x) \to -\infty$.
